SUMMARY:Scenic AVL - Hendersonville - with WNC American Pilgrims on the Ca
 mino
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of the associat
 ion of American Pilgrims on the Camino. The route has been announced on th
 e WNC Camino Group [Facebook Group Page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/A
 VLCamino/announcements).\nIf you are unfamiliar with the Camino\, here are
  a few links to learn more:\n\n\\*[American Pilgrims on the Camino](https:
 //americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory/western-north-carolina/)\n\n* [Sti
 ngy Nomads Camino](https://stingynomads.com/camino-de-santiago-walking-gui
 de/)\n\\*[Gronze Camino Planner](https://www.gronze.com/)\n* [https://en.w
 ikipedia.org/wiki/The_Way_(2010_film)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_W
 ay_(2010_film))\n\n**Distance:** 5\, 7\, or 11 miles\n**Pace: 3.2 mph**\n\
 n**Start Times**\n**9:30 am**\\- Meet at First Congregational Church\\\, 1
 735 5th Ave W\\\, Hendersonville\\\, NC\n**11:15 - 11:45 - Southern Stream
 s coffee across from the FCC church.**\n\nFirst Section: The first section
  is a five mile loop. The loop ends at Southern Streams coffee house\, whi
 ch is across from the church where we start. Join us here for coffee\, eve
 n if you don't have time to walk.\n\nSecond Section: Starting at about 11:
 45 am from Southern Streams coffee\, continue through lower Laurel Park. F
 or those who want to exit\, you can return to the church on the Ecusta Tra
 il for a total of about 7 miles.\n\nLast Section: To downtown and St. Jame
 s Church\, returning via Ecusta Trail. 10.5 miles total distance.\nThe chu
 rch historian will be on hand to give a brief history of the stained glass
  windows in the church. And we will have cake.\n\n**Caution:** There are a
  few stretches on busy roads where we will need to walk single file.\n\nFu
 ll Route: [Laurel Park Loop](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/map/laurel-
 park-loop-improved-3937230?u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\n\nParking: We are meeting at th
 e First Congregational Church. Please carpool if possible.\n\nDogs: On lea
 sh the entire time. The first section is shady\, but the pavement may be h
 ot on the last section. Please consider your pup's feet in the heat.\n\nSc
 enic Asheville Series: This hike counts as a Wildcard substitute on my Sce
 nic Asheville Series. There are 9 [hikes](https://docs.google.com/document
 /d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=drivesdk) in the 
 series\; hike them all and receive an [attractive badge](https://docs.goog
 le.com/drawings/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit) for y
 our backpack. Check your status [HERE](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheet
 s/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=0#gid=0).\n\n**Q
 uestions**\nIf you have questions\, call the hike leader (Gracen) at 828-2
 90-0886.\n\n**Guests:** For this hike\, there are no guest restrictions. B
 ring them with you.\n\n**Disclaimer and Release of Liability:**\nThis acti
 vity involves hiking on city streets that may have traffic and/or hiking o
 n natural surfaces. Participants are responsible for their safety on stree
 ts and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a profess
 ional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. 
 If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you freel
 y and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and 
 damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. Yo
 u are responsible for any guests\, dogs or other companions you bring with
  you. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [h
 ttps://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316598416
 /
