BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_316823501@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261003T050016Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T130000
SUMMARY:Bent Creek-Sidehill: 7 mi 1000 ft elev. gain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**[Sign-up opens Sunday\, Oct. 4th
 \, 8:00 pm]**\n\nThis is a "Todd Hike" that's mostly on Lower Sidehill Tra
 il and South Ridge Rd. It's a pretty area deep into Bent Creek. The plan i
 s for a "lollipop" with a short stem at the start and finish\, and a big l
 oop the rest of the way.\n\nBe prepared for a moderate pace\, around 2.4 m
 ph. There's good footing throughout\, with a combination of forest trails 
 and gravel roads. Ups and downs are relatively mild. If you're on the fenc
 e about poles\, you probably won't need them here. Bring water and\, if yo
 u're inclined\, a snack\, too. There'll be a little break somewhere around
  the middle.\n\n**CARPOOLING TIME & PLACE**\n\nThere's limited trailhead p
 arking\, so we'll carpool from the Asheville Outlets behind the Waffle Hou
 se (directions below). Look for me and my silver Hyundai. Come early to al
 low for traffic. We'll depart by 9:00 AM\n\nHere's the Waffle House locati
 on on Google Maps:\n[https://goo.gl/maps/kjkQTmGQA7QNgbWLA](https://goo.gl
 /maps/kjkQTmGQA7QNgbWLA)\n\n**From Exit 33 on I-26\,**\n\n* Head south a s
 hort distance on Brevard Rd. (Rt. 191) to the traffic light with Ingles on
  the right and Waffle House on the left.\n* Turn Left into the Asheville O
 utlets.\n* Drive just past the Waffle House and turn left onto the parking
  lot access road\, NOT into the Waffle House lot.\n* Take the first right.
  We'll park and meet in this area of the lot.\n\n**ALSO IMPORTANT**\n***Do
 gs.*** Well-behaved dogs are welcome\, but U.S. Forest Service regulations
  require leashes. Wear sensible hiking boots. Bring some water. If you're 
 on the fence about hiking poles\, you probably don't need them for this on
 e.\n\n***Guests.*** If you'd like to bring a guest\, they must join the As
 heville Hiking Group and sign up for the hike independently. Alternatively
 \, contact me in advance to ask if it's okay to bring a +1 after you've ma
 de it onto the "Going" list. Depending on timing and demand\, we may be ab
 le to add your guest.\n\n**COURTESY TO WAITLISTERS** (Please abide!)\nOnly
  sign up if you \\*truly\\* plan to come. And if you're on the borderline 
 of dropping out for any reason\, buck up and join us! I promise you'll be 
 glad you did.\n\nIf you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not Go
 ing" as soon as possible so wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And p
 lease please PLEASE don't ever be a "no-show" for any MeetUp events. Let y
 our organizer know in advance.\n\nIf you're on the waiting list\, keep che
 cking the evening before. Despite what I wrote above\, we usually have las
 t-minute dropouts.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather and post a cance
 llation message by 7:30 AM if the forecast is >50% chance of precipitation
 .\n\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**LEGALESE
 **\nThis Asheville Hiking Group (AHG) event involves hiking and\, possibly
 \, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsibl
 e for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, 
 physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks
  to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking
  Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume
  full responsibility for any damages or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316823501
 /
